  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Muon efficiency — V13/V17 \"clean\" filter\n",
    "\n",
    "Tests the hypothesis that the staircase dips in the muon KF efficiency vs $p_T$ are driven by particles whose **best KF fit fails to anchor a measurement on a truth-hit layer in volume 13 or 17**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The filtered curve is built from `attribute_holes_per_layer_all_gt.json[\"clean_eff\"]` (per-species `num`/`den` on the same 40-bin pT axis as `eff_per_particle.json`). A GT muon counts towards `num`/`den` iff it has at least one CKF attempt AND its best attempt has **zero** Mode-2 misses (truth-hit layer with no KF Measurement state) in V13 ∪ V17. Particles with no CKF attempt are excluded entirely.\n",
    "\n",
    "If the staircase disappears in the clean curve, V13/V17 misses fully explain it; residual dips indicate other failure modes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
