   "source": [
    "## KF Failure Modes — UNMATCHED GT Only (per-layer attribution)\n",
    "\n",
    "Re-attribution of holes & missed-truth-layers using only the **best KF attempt of GT particles that ended up unmatched**. This filters out holes belonging to tracks that still successfully reconstructed their particle (which inflated the original `kf_failure_modes.json` plots).\n",
    "\n",
    "Theoretical layer thresholds $p_T = 0.15 \\cdot B \\cdot R$ (B = 2 T) overlaid as triangles on the x-axis.\n",
    "\n",
    "Data produced by `acts/output_examples/attribute_holes_per_layer.py` (30 events) and saved to `attribute_holes_per_layer.json`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
