   "source": [
    "## Section: Muon hit-position on V17L2 vs V13L8\n",
    "\n",
    "GT-only diagnostic from `acts/output_examples/muon_position/`. Simulation: 100 events × 75 muons, $p_T \\in [0.2, 0.5]$ GeV, $\\eta \\approx 0$, $\\phi = 0$, random charge, $B_z = 2$ T.\n",
    "\n",
    "For each muon, take outgoing truth hits ($\\vec{p}_T \\cdot \\hat{r} > 0$) on two layers:\n",
    "- **V17L2** ($r \\approx 820$ mm) — outermost barrel reached by most muons in this $p_T$ range; threshold $p_T \\approx 0.246$ GeV.\n",
    "- **V13L8** ($r \\approx 660$ mm) — one layer inward; threshold $p_T \\approx 0.198$ GeV (below the simulated $p_T$ floor, so always reached).\n",
    "\n",
    "Plotted: mean hit $\\phi$ (and the arc displacement $s = r\\,\\phi$) on each layer per $p_T$ bin, for $q = -1$ only. Hypothesis: V17L2 starts showing the apex curvature blow-up as $p_T$ approaches 0.246 GeV, while V13L8 stays in the gentle linear regime through the whole $p_T$ range — so the V17L2 curve should diverge sharply at low $p_T$ while V13L8 stays flat-ish.\n"
   ]
  },
